# Standalone build: no backend services configured.
#
# Used for any deploy where this app is served as plain static files and cannot
# reach our signaling server — an itch.io upload, a subpath host, a fork without
# a server of its own. Build with:
#
#   npx vite build --mode standalone --base=./
#
# Multiplayer is gated on this being falsy (`main.ts`'s
# MULTIPLAYER_SERVER_CONFIGURED); `updateMultiplayerTabEnabled` then hides the
# tab entirely, so the build never advertises a mode it cannot connect.
#
# This file states intent in one greppable place. It is not a guarantee — Vite's precedence means a .env.standalone.local silently overrides it (measured: the Multiplayer tab came back). Only checking the built artifact holds.
VITE_MULTIPLAYER_SERVER_URL=
